CCAAVVEEAATTSS
       Do not use mmeemmccmmpp() to compare confidential data, such as cryptographic
       secrets, because the CPU time required for the comparison depends on
       the contents of the addresses compared, this function is subject to
       timing‐based side‐channel attacks.  In such cases, a function that
       performs comparisons in deterministic time, depending only on _n (the
       quantity of bytes compared) is required.  Some operating systems
       provide such a function (e.g., NetBSD’s ccoonnssttttiimmee__mmeemmeeqquuaall()), but no
       such function is specified in POSIX.  On Linux, you may need to
       implement such a function yourself.

